From e27a1e36bf12f8239a4e136beef55331d989c15b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chedy Souffargi <cs@karo-electronics.de>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 18:58:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: imx95-qs95: thermal trips for the industrial
 grade

The QS95-5610 carries an MIMX9556CVTXNAC, industrial grade: IMX95IEC
Rev.8 Table 23 gives Tj = -40 to 105 C. imx95.dtsi keeps the trips of
the 125 C grades: passive at 105 C and critical at 125 C for the A55
and ANA zones. The System Manager programs the TEMPSENSE panic
threshold from the market segment fuse, 107 C for the industrial part
(dev_sm_sensor.c, panicTemp[2]), and IMX95RM ch. 26 routes that
threshold "To SRC and FCCU only": a hardware reset, no software path.

So throttling started at the junction limit, 2 C before a hard reset,
and the critical trip could never be reached. Move the passive trips to
95 C and the critical ones to 105 C for both zones.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 .../boot/dts/freescale/imx95-qs95-5610.dts      | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95-qs95-5610.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95-qs95-5610.dts
index b8d753123de0..34979ab5c30b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95-qs95-5610.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95-qs95-5610.dts
@@ -318,6 +318,23 @@ IMX95_PAD_SD1_STROBE__USDHC1_STROBE			0x15fe
 	};
 };
 
+/* Tj max 105 C industrial (IMX95IEC Tab.23); SM resets at 107 C */
+&cpu_alert0 {
+	temperature = <95000>;
+};
+
+&cpu_crit0 {
+	temperature = <105000>;
+};
+
+&ana_alert {
+	temperature = <95000>;
+};
+
+&ana_crit0 {
+	temperature = <105000>;
+};
+
 &thermal_zones {
 	a55-thermal {
 		trips {
-- 
2.43.0

